FREE AT LAST from this infernal game - at least version 3.0.x, because I
MADE IT! Shumpfy the Valkyrie, 22nd level, with big assists from two
bones levels from earlier characters (one of whom was a wizard and so
provided a couple of key items from his stash).

I have to say I agree with those who say the game is unbalanced: the
most interesting and challenging (infuriating!) part is the first 20
levels or so - that's where the game is really addictive. Once you're
strong enough to make it past the castle and make good use of that wand
of wishing, Hell is merely tedious, until you find the Wiz. The Wiz is
annoying until you paralyze him (3.0.9), but there is *NO* good reason
to have 20 levels of Hell. Boring. The endlevel is, if you have a ring
of conflict, simply silly. Even without one it sort of is, actually; I
mean, a room of liches followed by a room of dragons followed by a room
of...OGRES??? I about died laughing. I had previously made it to the
endlevel without a ring of conflict, and with the Wiz still on my tail,
and I got slaughtered - had no chance at all, with an even more powerful
character than this one. So the difference of that one item was very
drastic, too much I think. And there ought to be *some* way to dispatch
the Wiz, or at least stall him for long enough to have a fihting chance
in the end level. I think if the r.o.conflict is weakened (which seems
necessary) but the Wiz can no longer be paralyzed, the end level will be
too much.

Vlad's Tower is irrelevant; I didn't even bother with it, because I had
the Amulet and there is no special reward from the Tower.

One curiosity: in my copy of the Wheaton Spoilers there is a "big room"
level described. In all my time playing I've never seen one. Is it
unimplemented?

It doesn't make sense that my chaotic Valkyrie was able to make
donations for armor class bonuses to a lawful priestess. On the other
hand I think there should one temple of each alignment in every game.

There ought to be at least one of every kind of shop scattered through
every game, but they should be much harder to steal from. This would,
for one thing, make gold much more meaningful. Right now, unless there's
a temple and/or you really care about your final score, gold and gems
become pretty irrelevant before very long.

Hopefully version 3.1 will have more special rooms, more
quests-within-the-quest (like the castle and Vlad's Tower, only better
designed), far fewer levels of Hell, and so on.
Or maybe it shouldn't. Cause if it does I might waste some more months
on this game!!!!

